- [Crow] George Kaplan.

254
00:10:00,500 --> 00:10:02,467
- Alexander Phipps.

255
00:10:02,467 --> 00:10:04,700
- Alexander Phipps?

256
00:10:04,700 --> 00:10:05,900
Sounds revolting.

257
00:10:05,900 --> 00:10:07,400
- [Tom] Sounds
Montclair momenty.

258
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:09,600
- Whatever my dear brother
think I'd be interested

259
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:11,400
in a character with
a name like that?

260
00:10:11,400 --> 00:10:13,267
- [Tom] Well you throw
yourself with anything with a--

261
00:10:13,267 --> 00:10:15,433
- As far as Mr. Alexander
Phipps is concerned,

262
00:10:15,433 --> 00:10:17,367
he'll be left alone.

263
00:10:17,367 --> 00:10:18,200
- [Tom] Permanently (laughs).

264
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:19,567
- Strictly alone.

265
00:10:19,567 --> 00:10:21,200
And with the
greatest of pleasure.

266
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:24,233
- [Crow] More food, hide
the pain, more food.

267
00:10:24,233 --> 00:10:25,267
Mmm, muenster.

268
00:10:28,067 --> 00:10:29,867
- [Tom] The patio only
sees the sides a girl can

269
00:10:29,867 --> 00:10:31,167
see from Brooklyn Heights, hey!

270
00:10:31,167 --> 00:10:32,200
Whoa, the crazy--

271
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:36,033
- [Mike] Hey, the young
Milly Helper chronicles.

272
00:10:36,033 --> 00:10:37,233
- Judy.

273
00:10:37,233 --> 00:10:38,600
Is it about time you've
got dressed dear?

274
00:10:38,600 --> 00:10:39,867
- I'm dressed.

275
00:10:39,867 --> 00:10:41,633
- Well that's a
matter of opinion.

276
00:10:41,633 --> 00:10:43,733
Go put on a dress
before they get here.

277
00:10:43,733 --> 00:10:45,467
- Ah, for him?

278
00:10:45,467 --> 00:10:49,067
Okay but nobody named Alexander
Phipps would ever notice

279
00:10:49,067 --> 00:10:49,900
what I had on.

280
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:51,200
(car horn beeps)

281
00:10:51,200 --> 00:10:52,033
- [Crow] Yeah, if you're
named Alexander Phipps,

282
00:10:52,033 --> 00:10:54,033
it's just over for ya.

283
00:10:54,033 --> 00:10:55,800
- [Tom] Wow, the
bacon truck is here.

284
00:10:55,800 --> 00:10:56,633
- Jeepers!

285
00:10:56,633 --> 00:10:57,533
Is he cool!

286
00:10:59,433 --> 00:11:00,700
Really cool!

287
00:11:00,700 --> 00:11:01,967
- [Crow] Tonight's
the night Mom!

288
00:11:01,967 --> 00:11:03,467
- Mother!

289
00:11:03,467 --> 00:11:06,500
They're here and look
at me, I'm a mess.

290
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:09,000
- Oh, why do you care, remember?

291
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,733
His name is Alexander Phipps.

292
00:11:11,733 --> 00:11:15,267
- Oh, wait 'til I get that
brother of mine alone.

293
00:11:15,267 --> 00:11:18,167
(bright music)

294
00:11:18,167 --> 00:11:20,033
- [Tom] Jeez, it's
Chip and Dale.

295
00:11:20,033 --> 00:11:22,033
- [Crow] Would you
just get in the door.

296
00:11:24,733 --> 00:11:25,800
- Hi, Mom.

297
00:11:25,800 --> 00:11:26,800
- [Tom] I'm back from the 20s.

298
00:11:26,800 --> 00:11:28,033
- Gee it's good to be home.

299
00:11:28,033 --> 00:11:29,767
- [Crow] Had to be
Robert McNamara.

300
00:11:29,767 --> 00:11:31,633
- Mom, this is Alex.

301
00:11:31,633 --> 00:11:34,433
- [Mom] Hello, Alex, we're
very happy to have you with us.

302
00:11:34,433 --> 00:11:37,300
- Oh thank you Mrs. Adams,
it's nice of you to have me.

303
00:11:37,300 --> 00:11:38,633
- [Crow] It's nice to be had.

304
00:11:38,633 --> 00:11:40,500
- Wait a minute, don't tell me.

305
00:11:40,500 --> 00:11:42,400
You're the twin
without the Tony.

306
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:45,200
- [Tom] Ah, go sit on
a carrot you crummy.

307
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:47,733
- Alex this is the little
sister I was telling you about.

308
00:11:47,733 --> 00:11:49,900
Judy, Alexander Phipps.

309
00:11:49,900 --> 00:11:51,667
- How do you do Mr. Phipps?

310
00:11:51,667 --> 00:11:53,100
So nice you could come.

311
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:54,433
- Well thanks, Judy.

312
00:11:54,433 --> 00:11:55,633
And the name is Alex.

313
00:11:55,633 --> 00:11:56,600
- [Tom] Xander Phipps.

314
00:11:56,600 --> 00:11:58,067
- Did you boys have your lunch?

315
00:11:58,067 --> 00:12:01,167
- Oh no, we didn't want to
miss another one of your meals.

316
00:12:01,167 --> 00:12:03,133
Besides, we wanted
to catch a shower.

317
00:12:03,133 --> 00:12:04,167
- [Mike] Wow.

318
00:12:04,167 --> 00:12:05,700
- Well okay, come along then.

319
00:12:05,700 --> 00:12:06,900
I'll have everything ready
by the time you get back.

320
00:12:06,900 --> 00:12:09,067
- [Crow] Join us
later if you want, Ma.

321
00:12:09,067 --> 00:12:11,800
- Oh, Mom, how bout some of
those hot biscuits of yours?

322
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:12,767
- [Mike] Whoa, my God.

323
00:12:12,767 --> 00:12:13,700
- All right, hot biscuits.

324
00:12:13,700 --> 00:12:14,967
Judy will make them for you.

325
00:12:14,967 --> 00:12:15,967
- Judy?

326
00:12:15,967 --> 00:12:18,033
I didn't know she could--

327
00:12:18,033 --> 00:12:18,900
- [Tom] Biscuit!

328
00:12:18,900 --> 00:12:20,100
- Come on up.

329
00:12:20,100 --> 00:12:21,567
- Oh, that sounds
real good, and thanks.

330
00:12:21,567 --> 00:12:23,967
- [Crow] Hee, I'll
soap ya first!

331
00:12:23,967 --> 00:12:26,567
- Mother, you do
the biscuits huh?

332
00:12:26,567 --> 00:12:28,567
- Well it'll only take
you a moment Judy.

333
00:12:28,567 --> 00:12:29,700
- Thanks Angel.

334
00:12:29,700 --> 00:12:31,700
I think I will throw on a dress.

335
00:12:31,700 --> 00:12:33,200
More lady like
don't you think so?

336
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:34,400
- Yes dear.

337
00:12:34,400 --> 00:12:36,700
But Alexander Phipps
will never notice that.

338
00:12:36,700 --> 00:12:39,033
- You're a doll mother.

339
00:12:39,033 --> 00:12:40,267
- [Tom] Now make the biscuits.

340
00:12:40,267 --> 00:12:43,400
- [Crow] You can hardly
see where you bit me.

341
00:12:43,400 --> 00:12:45,867
- Sure do get a smooth shave
with this electric razor.

342
00:12:45,867 --> 00:12:47,500
Hope your dad won't mind.

343
00:12:47,500 --> 00:12:49,433
- [Bob] Nah, he
won't mind a bit.

344
00:12:49,433 --> 00:12:51,533
He always lets me
use it when I'm home.

345
00:12:51,533 --> 00:12:53,467
Dad's a swell guy,
you'll like him.

346
00:12:53,467 --> 00:12:55,967
- [Tom] Just don't use his
razor, he goes ballistic!

347
00:12:55,967 --> 00:12:59,267
- Hey, you're not running
out of hot water are you?

348
00:12:59,267 --> 00:13:00,833
- What?

349
00:13:00,833 --> 00:13:03,300
- I said you're not running
out of hot water are you?

350
00:13:03,300 --> 00:13:05,133
I stayed under
quite a long time.

351
00:13:05,133 --> 00:13:06,067
- [Mike] Wow.

352
00:13:06,067 --> 00:13:07,500
- Oh don't worry about that,

353
00:13:07,500 --> 00:13:09,500
wait 'til you see the electric
water heater dad got us.

354
00:13:09,500 --> 00:13:12,267
We're loaded now, we have plenty
of hot water all the time.

355
00:13:12,267 --> 00:13:14,700
- [Crow] Sounds fun, I
gotta get outta here.

356
00:13:14,700 --> 00:13:16,367
- Hey, Bob.

357
00:13:16,367 --> 00:13:17,833
- [Bob] Yeah?

358
00:13:17,833 --> 00:13:19,633
- I thought you said your
sister was just a little kid?

359
00:13:19,633 --> 00:13:20,767
- [Tom] She must be 40.

360
00:13:20,767 --> 00:13:21,900
- [Bob] Don't let her fool ya.

361
00:13:21,900 --> 00:13:23,267
She's still a little monster.

362
00:13:23,267 --> 00:13:24,767
- [Mike] I'm the beast master.

363
00:13:27,400 --> 00:13:29,933
- [Crow] There, now
I look like Mom.

364
00:13:29,933 --> 00:13:32,500
Well thank goodness
for my electric dress.

365
00:13:34,033 --> 00:13:35,600
- [Tom] Hey where's
the fire extinguisher?

366
00:13:37,167 --> 00:13:40,067
- [Mike] He'll never touch
you Terry you're dirt.

367
00:13:41,267 --> 00:13:42,900
- Hey, you look might purty.

368
00:13:42,900 --> 00:13:43,933
- [Mike] In a Thelma
Retter sort of way.

369
00:13:43,933 --> 00:13:45,667
- Now about that food.

370
00:13:45,667 --> 00:13:48,867
- Food, is that all you can
think of at a time like this?

371
00:13:48,867 --> 00:13:49,900
- [Crow] Ya mean lunchtime?

372
00:13:49,900 --> 00:13:52,333
- Don't change the subject.

373
00:13:52,333 --> 00:13:55,200
I ought to wring your
smug little neck.

374
00:13:55,200 --> 00:13:57,200
- What's the matter
now, what have I done?

375
00:13:57,200 --> 00:13:59,833
- Studious, serious minded.

376
00:13:59,833 --> 00:14:01,600
- What are you talking about?

377
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:03,433
- Tops in all his classes.

378
00:14:03,433 --> 00:14:04,667
- [Crow] Point, counter point.

379
00:14:04,667 --> 00:14:06,767
- Now Judy, Alex
is really a guy--

380
00:14:06,767 --> 00:14:08,067
- Who has little time for girls.

381
00:14:08,067 --> 00:14:09,833
- Now wait a minute,
let me explain.

382
00:14:09,833 --> 00:14:11,667
- And a woman hater to boot.

383
00:14:11,667 --> 00:14:14,767
I think you're a stinker!

384
00:14:14,767 --> 00:14:16,100
- [Crow] No, don't.

385
00:14:16,100 --> 00:14:17,700
- Why do girls have
to have brothers?

386
00:14:17,700 --> 00:14:19,200
- I love you too.

387
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:21,833
Now simmer down
sis, it's the truth.

388
00:14:21,833 --> 00:14:23,367
- [Mike] What a loser

389
00:14:23,367 --> 00:14:26,400
- Alex really has no time
for girls, especially you.

390
00:14:26,400 --> 00:14:29,533
- Flattery will get you nowhere.

391
00:14:29,533 --> 00:14:31,533
Just watch junior.

392
00:14:31,533 --> 00:14:32,367
- [Mike] Doom, doom,
god I hate women.

393
00:14:32,367 --> 00:14:33,567
Oh hi!

394
00:14:33,567 --> 00:14:34,600
- Hi, Alex.

395
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:35,633
I know you're hungry.

396
00:14:35,633 --> 00:14:37,467
You'll be eating in a jiffy.

397
00:14:37,467 --> 00:14:38,300
Excuse me.

398
00:14:39,333 --> 00:14:40,167
- [Crow] Ah, my new kidney.

399
00:14:43,633 --> 00:14:44,767
Oh, one of them Insinkerators.

400
00:14:44,767 --> 00:14:46,500
- [Mom] Everything's
ready, Judy.

401
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:47,867
- Come and get it.

402
00:14:47,867 --> 00:14:51,700
(Tom imitates choking)

403
00:14:51,700 --> 00:14:53,333
- [Crow] Hey, make
with the cha broads.

404
00:14:53,333 --> 00:14:54,600
- Sit down boys.

405
00:14:54,600 --> 00:14:56,133
- C'mon Alex, make
yourself at home.

406
00:14:56,133 --> 00:14:57,033
- Sorry to put you to all
this trouble, Mrs. Adams,

407
00:14:57,033 --> 00:14:58,933
but it does smell good.

408
00:14:58,933 --> 00:15:00,333
- No trouble at all, Alex.

409
00:15:00,333 --> 00:15:03,000
Everything's so easy
with an electric range.

410
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:07,333
Possibly I'm prejudice but seems
the food tastes better too.

411
00:15:07,333 --> 00:15:10,233
- Say, I hate to corny
but what's cooking?

412
00:15:10,233 --> 00:15:11,967
- Stew, beef stew.

413
00:15:11,967 --> 00:15:14,067
Mom knows how you love it.

414
00:15:15,267 --> 00:15:16,833
- Wonderful, it's
my favorite dish.

415
00:15:16,833 --> 00:15:19,800
- [Mike] Well, used to be
my favorite dish, Jesus.

416
00:15:19,800 --> 00:15:21,500
- [Crow] You got a claw
hammer or something I can

417
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:22,400
work on this with?

418
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:24,233
- Hot biscuits.

419
00:15:24,233 --> 00:15:25,200
Mother made them.

420
00:15:26,067 --> 00:15:27,767
- [Crow] Hey the electric phone!

421
00:15:27,767 --> 00:15:29,167
- I'll get it Mom.

422
00:15:29,167 --> 00:15:30,833
- Throw some of
these tomatoes on.

423
00:15:30,833 --> 00:15:32,033
- Thanks.

424
00:15:32,033 --> 00:15:33,500
- [Tom] Dad's calling
from Chippendales.

425
00:15:33,500 --> 00:15:35,367
They got two shows,
he won't be home.

426
00:15:37,133 --> 00:15:39,000
- More Similac dear?

427
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:40,500
- Did he arrive?

428
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:42,600
Man he's positively frantic.

429
00:15:42,600 --> 00:15:43,833
- [Crow] He runs
around screaming.

430
00:15:43,833 --> 00:15:45,533
- He's a real cool Jonah.

431
00:15:45,533 --> 00:15:49,200
Tall, good looking,
nothing at all like the

432
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:50,667
drips around school.

433
00:15:50,667 --> 00:15:52,467
- [Tom] If you'd like to
make a call please hang up--

434
00:15:52,467 --> 00:15:53,733
- Uh huh.

435
00:15:53,733 --> 00:15:56,333
And he drives a real
shafty convertible.

436
00:15:56,333 --> 00:15:57,900
He really has it.

437
00:15:57,900 --> 00:15:59,033
- [Tom] And I want it.

438
00:15:59,033 --> 00:16:00,400
- Oh when he looks at me I get,

439
00:16:00,400 --> 00:16:02,200
you know squishy.

440
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:03,467
- [Mike] Oh that's nice ma'am,

441
00:16:03,467 --> 00:16:04,633
I'm just trying to
sell my magazines.

442
00:16:04,633 --> 00:16:05,567
- This afternoon?

443
00:16:05,567 --> 00:16:07,100
Oh that's a wonderful idea.

444
00:16:07,100 --> 00:16:08,167
- [Crow] Have my way with him?

445
00:16:08,167 --> 00:16:09,367
- What time?

446
00:16:09,367 --> 00:16:10,233
Okay.

447
00:16:10,233 --> 00:16:11,733
Bye!

448
00:16:11,733 --> 00:16:13,833
- Well that stew was really
a production, Mrs. Adams.

449
00:16:13,833 --> 00:16:15,100
Can we help with the dishes?

450
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:18,300
- Ah, no KT duty
around here, Sergeant.

451
00:16:18,300 --> 00:16:20,300
- [Tom] We got dames to do that.

452
00:16:20,300 --> 00:16:21,900
- Strictly automatic, see?

453
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:25,633
Oops.

454
00:16:25,633 --> 00:16:26,567
- [Tom] Found the smell.

455
00:16:26,567 --> 00:16:27,367
- Some in here already Mom.

456
00:16:27,367 --> 00:16:28,367
- That's all right dear,

457
00:16:28,367 --> 00:16:29,633
just put them in
with the others.

458
00:16:29,633 --> 00:16:30,500
- [Crow] Why what are
all these gin bottles

459
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:31,333
doing in here?

460
00:16:33,067 --> 00:16:35,433
- Oh wait a minute, Bob,
why not do it the easy way?

461
00:16:35,433 --> 00:16:37,133
- [Tom] You're suffocating me.

462
00:16:37,133 --> 00:16:38,067
- Excuse me, Mom.

463
00:16:38,067 --> 00:16:39,433
- [Crow] It's Pepperidge Farm.

464
00:16:39,433 --> 00:16:41,200
- That used to be
my job at home,

465
00:16:41,200 --> 00:16:42,900
washing the dishes I mean.

466
00:16:42,900 --> 00:16:45,933
- Oh, Bob and Judy have
had their share too.

467
00:16:45,933 --> 00:16:47,633
But thank heaven, no
more wiping and wiping

468
00:16:47,633 --> 00:16:48,833
dishes around here.

469
00:16:48,833 --> 00:16:50,800
- [Crow] God your
hair smells terrific.

470
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:52,700
- And the dishwater
uses such hot water,

471
00:16:52,700 --> 00:16:55,067
you couldn't possibly
put your hands in it.

472
00:16:55,067 --> 00:16:58,567
- Sure, that makes the
dishes hygienically clean.

473
00:16:58,567 --> 00:17:00,933
- I'll put the Heatwell cooker
in when I do the next load.

474
00:17:00,933 --> 00:17:02,200
- [Crow] I've never felt so

475
00:17:02,200 --> 00:17:04,100
comfortable with a
woman, Mrs. Adams.

476
00:17:04,100 --> 00:17:05,367
Alexander please.

477
00:17:05,367 --> 00:17:06,800
Do you want to have
breakfast sometime?

478
00:17:06,800 --> 00:17:08,633
Don't do this to me Alexander.

479
00:17:11,967 --> 00:17:13,467
- See, nothing to it is there?

480
00:17:13,467 --> 00:17:14,833
- [Tom] And it's quiet too!

481
00:17:16,233 --> 00:17:18,667
- [Crow] Eleanor, I'm busy
down here at the White House.

482
00:17:18,667 --> 00:17:19,900
- Okay beautiful.

483
00:17:19,900 --> 00:17:21,833
Now don't forget to
call me, will ya?

484
00:17:22,767 --> 00:17:23,700
Right.

485
00:17:23,700 --> 00:17:25,233
- [Crow] Good bye, Eleanor.

486
00:17:25,233 --> 00:17:27,600
- Sally phoned and asked
me to go for a swim.

487
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:29,867
Thought you might
like to come along.

488
00:17:29,867 --> 00:17:31,533
And bring Alex.

489
00:17:31,533 --> 00:17:33,167
- Oh, thanks.

490
00:17:33,167 --> 00:17:35,200
But I think Alex is
going to be busy.

491
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:36,867
- Busy doing what?

492
00:17:36,867 --> 00:17:39,900
- Now look small fry,
don't give me any trouble.

493
00:17:39,900 --> 00:17:42,100
All I know is he's
seeing a man at the

494
00:17:42,100 --> 00:17:44,767
Northwest Machine Works on
the matter of hydraulics.

495
00:17:44,767 --> 00:17:46,000
- [Tom] Say.

496
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:46,933
- Why don't you
ask him yourself?

497
00:17:46,933 --> 00:17:49,000
- Thanks, I will.

498
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:51,300
- [Mike] I'm squishy and
I need to move on it.

499
00:17:53,133 --> 00:17:55,000
- And the circulating air
completely dries them.

500
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:56,467
- [Crow] Please
stop I'm vulnerable.

501
00:17:56,467 --> 00:17:58,100
- You certainly know
all about dishwashers.

502
00:17:58,100 --> 00:18:00,700
- Oh not all, but to tell
the truth Mrs. Adams,

503
00:18:00,700 --> 00:18:03,700
anything of mechanical or
electrical nature interests me.

504
00:18:03,700 --> 00:18:05,600
Fits in with a hobby of mine.

505
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:06,867
- Dishwashers?

506
00:18:06,867 --> 00:18:07,967
- Not exactly.

507
00:18:07,967 --> 00:18:09,200
